.TH TAEMA-AGENT 1 "2026-10-30" "taema 1.0.0" "Tæma Manual"
.SH NAME
taema agent \- relay this session's desktop facts to the tæma daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taema agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
The session agent runs once per graphical session and relays desktop facts
to the per-user daemon, which keeps every decision. The agent itself decides
nothing: it streams window open, change, close, and focus facts from the
compositor, reports notification actions and launch requests, and polls the
daemon's notification queue through the configured backend.
.PP
Only one agent runs per session, held under a lock. On start it joins the
protected
.I agent
leaf (asking the daemon to attach it only when a direct move fails),
registers its capabilities, and beats every 30 seconds with exponential
reconnect backoff capped at 30 seconds. The daemon accepts
.I register_agent
and
.I agent_beat
only from the same uid, marks agents down after 3 missed beats with
.I agent_up
and
.I agent_down
audit events, and refuses stale facts so it decides on process data only.
The agent exits when the compositor socket goes away. The agent leaf is
never adopted, frozen, deprioritized, reclaimed, undone, stopped, or
removed.
.PP
Without an agent, or without an action-capable notification server, reviews
wait for the shell hint and
.BR taema review .
Killing the agent degrades the daemon to process-only mode without errors,
and a restarted agent re-registers within 30 seconds.
.SH SESSION SETUP
The agent needs a Wayland compositor socket. For niri, start it from the
compositor configuration:
.PP
.RS
spawn-at-startup "taema" "agent"
.RE
.PP
An example snippet ships under
.IR /usr/share/examples/taema/autostart/niri-taema-agent.kdl ,
with an XDG autostart entry
.IR taema-agent.desktop
alongside it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/examples/taema/autostart/niri-taema-agent.kdl
Example niri
.I spawn-at-startup
entry.
.TP
.I /usr/share/examples/taema/autostart/taema-agent.desktop
XDG autostart entry for desktop environments that honour it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR taema (1),
.BR taema.toml (5)
